Ctrl+C / stray right-arrow key

Yes, this is fixable at the code level, independent of the hardware quirk. What's happening: the stray key sends a raw ANSI escape sequence (\x1b[C), and it's leaking into input() as literal characters instead of being consumed as a cursor-move — so it lands in the confirm-prompt answer or the next-goal string. The fix is to sanitize input right after reading it: strip ANSI/escape sequences (regex for \x1b\[[0-9;]*[a-zA-Z]) before comparing against "y"/"yes" or before sending a goal string to the API. That would turn a corrupted "\x1b[Cy" back into a clean "y", and a corrupted goal string back into clean text. Doesn't fix the flaky key itself, but neutralizes its effect on the pipeline. Want me to add this to the confirm-prompt and next-goal input points in robot_executor.py/thinkpad_robot_capture_to_amd.py?

