turn_speed/forward_speed validation — what to do

Given /high_state is confirmed working, use it directly instead of tape-measure/protractor methods:

1. rostopic echo -n 1 /high_state right before a test pulse — note position (x,y) and imu.rpy[2] (yaw).
2. Run one known pulse in an open area — e.g. --test-forward --forward-pulse-duration 2.0 for a forward test, --test-left for a turn test (note the actual total duration printed in the log, since long pulses get chunked).
3. rostopic echo -n 1 /high_state again once fully stopped — note position/yaw again.
4. Forward speed: actual_speed = sqrt((x1-x0)² + (y1-y0)²) / actual_duration, compare to the --forward-speed you passed.
5. Turn speed: actual_angle = yaw1 - yaw0 (wrap-correct: if the difference exceeds ±π, add/subtract 2π), actual_turn_speed = actual_angle / actual_duration, compare to --turn-speed.
6. Repeat 2-3 times each direction and average — legged-robot gait has some run-to-run variance.
7. Update --forward-speed/--turn-speed to whatever you actually measured.

This is also effectively a manual dry-run of what #4 would automate, so doing it now is useful groundwork either way.

